/**
 * Library Management System — single-file edition.
 *
 * This is a condensed, single-file version of a multi-package Java project,
 * made to paste-and-run on online Java compilers (OneCompiler, JDoodle,
 * Replit, Programiz, etc.) that only accept one file and give you a plain
 * stdin/stdout console.
 *
 * Two things were simplified to make that possible:
 *   1. Persistence is in-memory only (no data/*.txt files) — online compilers
 *      don't give you a persistent filesystem between runs anyway, so nothing
 *      is lost by dropping file storage. Sample data is re-seeded every run.
 *   2. Logging goes to the console instead of logs/library.log, since most
 *      online compilers don't let you read files back out after the run.
 *
 * Everything else — validation rules, custom exceptions, fine calculation,
 * the 3 functional modules (Members / Books / Issue-Return) — is unchanged.
 *
 * How to run here: paste this whole file into the compiler as
 * LibraryManagementSystem.java (the public class name must match the file
 * name) and run it. If the compiler has a separate "stdin" box, use it to
 * type menu choices; otherwise type directly into the console.
 */
public class LibraryManagementSystem {

